uestion-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u \\\\ {u}^{3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡u\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 3{u}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u(t)) \\\\ 3(u(t))^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{u(t)}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3({e}^{t})^{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{t}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ 3{e}^{2t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({e}^{t}){e}^{t} \\\\ 3{e}^{3t} \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-70695" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({e}^{2t}) \\\\ {e}^{3t} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{e}^{2t}}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(v(t)f(t))^{′}$ given that  $f(t)=⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩$ and $v(t)=\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n(v(t)f(t))^{′}=v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${v}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({2}^{2t}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩ \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}})=-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(v(t)f(t))^{′} & =v(t){f}^{′}(t)+{v}^{′}(t)f(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟨{2}^{t},\\,{2}^{t+1},\\,{2}^{2t}+1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{2\\cdot {2}^{2t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩-⟨\\frac{{2}^{t}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{{2}^{t+1}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}+1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "571886996c7160eb868c66716ca2bf5b6181089cb1e0b1f6808ce7ad8466ecd6" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}},\\,0⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,-\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{2}^{t},\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33446" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,\\,0,\\,\\frac{({2}^{2t}-1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{{2}^{t}}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/state.json" "file_sha256" "def595c30148f3efaa0dc0eea3ee6d376383e94ed4a1f5576887f7fc6d48fdf5" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t)$ with respect to $t,$ where $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)$ are defined as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i-(\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k \\\\ g(t) & =(4t-1)\\,i+{e}^{3t}\\,j+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "e486489bcd5484ab04f53931e3f20b0f707b556a45827a11e9d1c1398e737358" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2477" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f(t) + 2\\mathbf g(t))' = \\mathbf f'(t) + 2\\mathbf g'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{2}+9)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{t-2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,k \\\\  & =8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k, \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-1)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{3t})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)k \\\\  & =4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+2g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+2{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(8t\\,i+\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k)+2(4\\,i+3{e}^{3t}\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k) \\\\  & =8(t+1)\\,i+(\\frac{1}{(t-2)^{2}}+6{e}^{3t})\\,j-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2477.json" "file_sha256" "e486489bcd5484ab04f53931e3f20b0f707b556a45827a11e9d1c1398e737358" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)'$ where ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/assets/9e23d542bfc56d506f5437a35a92c304d618109ef60086e1f5a7a4fee57d8a80.png) and $u(t) = t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "7b59206f462607763175be7854fb0a196b73b152c6c3a237c00662dea0703dbd" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2478" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\big( u(t) \\mathbf g(t) \\big)' = u'(t) \\mathbf{g}(t) + u(t) \\mathbf{g}'(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find $\\mathbf g'(t)$ and $u'(t),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)g(t)+u(t){g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+t\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t} \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -t \\\\ {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -t \\\\ 2t{e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\ -2t \\\\ (2t+1){e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2478.json" "file_sha256" "7b59206f462607763175be7854fb0a196b73b152c6c3a237c00662dea0703dbd" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t),$ if $\\mathbf f(u) = \\ln u \\, \\mathbf i + (u^2+5) \\, \\mathbf j + 4u \\, \\mathbf k$ and $u(t) =2t^3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "28113e7a91a4858d2ab3461a832857115faa3dc19fd301b887c67984514497d7" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2479" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have \n\n$$\n(\\mathbf f \\circ u)'(t) = \\mathbf{f}'(u(t)) u'(t).\n$$\n\nNow, let's find the derivative of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡u)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({u}^{2}+5)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(4u)k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{u}\\,i+2u\\,j+4\\,k, \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3})=6{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{u(t)}\\,i+2u(t)\\,j+4\\,k){u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2{t}^{3}}\\,i+2(2{t}^{3})\\,j+4\\,k)\\cdot 6{t}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{t}\\,i+24{t}^{5}\\,j+24{t}^{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2479.json" "file_sha256" "28113e7a91a4858d2ab3461a832857115faa3dc19fd301b887c67984514497d7" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t),$ given the following functions $\\mathbf f(t)$ and $\\mathbf g(t)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =\\sqrt{t}\\,i+{t}^{2}j \\\\ g(t) & =\\frac{1}{t}i+{e}^{t}j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "d8de8779c3fe7edcf26858e8ab54c8123e41f02ec47535501cb0ba6221b2cc97" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-2480" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f} \\cdot \\mathbf{g})(t) = \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t))\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}f(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})j \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\,i+2t\\,j, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}g(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})j \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,i+{e}^{t}\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt} (\\mathbf f \\cdot \\mathbf g)(t)\n&= \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{f}(t)) \\cdot \\mathbf{g}(t) + \\mathbf{f}(t) \\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d}{\\textrm dt}(\\mathbf{g}(t)) \\[3pt]\n&= \\left(\\dfrac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} \\,\\mathbf i +2t \\, \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(\\dfrac{1}{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + e^t \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) +\n\\left(\\sqrt{t} \\,  \\mathbf i + t^2 \\,  \\mathbf j \\right) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{1}{t^2}  \\, \\mathbf i + e^t \\, \\mathbf j  \\right) \\[3pt]\t\t \n&=\\dfrac{1}{2t\\sqrt{t}}  +2te^t    +  \\left(-\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2}\\right)    + t^2e^t \\[3pt]\n&=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2}  -  \\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{t^2} +2te^t   + t^2e^t  \\[3pt]\n&= -\\dfrac{\\sqrt{t}}{2t^2} +\\left(2t+t^2\\right)e^t.\n}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/example-2480.json" "file_sha256" "d8de8779c3fe7edcf26858e8ab54c8123e41f02ec47535501cb0ba6221b2cc97" "basis" 1709 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14048749/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k \\\\ g(t) & ={t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the dot product rule, we can write:\n\n$$\n(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(20t)\\,i-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2+5t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+t)\\,k \\\\  & =3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f\\cdot g)^{′}(t) & ={f}^{′}(t)\\cdot g(t)+f(t)\\cdot {g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(20\\,i-2\\,j+5\\,k)\\cdot ({t}^{3}\\,i+t\\,j+({t}^{2}+t)\\,k)+(20t\\,i-2t\\,j+(2+5t)\\,k)\\cdot (3{t}^{2}\\,i+j+(2t+1)\\,k) \\\\  & =(20{t}^{3}-2t+5({t}^{2}+t))+(60{t}^{3}-2t+(2+5t)(2t+1)) \\\\  & =80{t}^{3}+15{t}^{2}+10t+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-32298" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)={e}^{u+1}\\,i+{e}^{2u}\\,j+\\frac{1}{e}\\,k$ and $u(t)=2{t}^{2}$ then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the chain rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)=f′(u(t))u′(t)\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{u+1})\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}({e}^{2u})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\frac{1}{e}\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2u}\\,j+0\\,k \\\\  & ={e}^{u+1}\\,i+2{e}^{2t}\\,j \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{2})=4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\ (f∘u)^{′}(t) & =({e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+2{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j)4t \\\\  & =4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-33260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "4t{e}^{2{t}^{2}+1}\\,i+8t{e}^{4{t}^{2}}\\,j"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb