athacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-71230" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}3{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ -16t \\\\ -{t}^{3}{e}^{-t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(u)=[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ {u}^{2} \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}$, then $(f∘u)^{′}(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the chain rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(f∘u)^{′}(t)={f}^{′}(u(t)){u}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(u) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(u) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}\\,({u}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}u}(6)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f∘u)^{′}(t) & =f′(u(t))u′(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2u(t) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {u}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2({e}^{t}) \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {e}^{t} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a9aaeb90fd4a53fb37b66163cbc9be084c3db1424222f7d7d46b1d07889cf311" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-128572" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/state.json" "file_sha256" "80b29861bd2fa46de813557573d447b9f281149e217ea52b4c7b80362a094ce8" "basis" 2512 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14070873/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-128144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}$ at $t=1,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-2g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-2{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(1)-2g(1))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(1)-2{g}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =⟨2(1),\\,\\frac{1}{1},\\,{e}^{1-1}⟩-2⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}},\\,3(1)^{2},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-2⟨1,3,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,1,1⟩-⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-128144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-2,-5,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-5,1⟩"] ["math" "⟨0,-7,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,7,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨4,7,9⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨0,-5,1⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨3t-1,\\,6-t,\\,7t⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2},\\,t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6-t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(7t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-{t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-1,\\,7⟩+⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t+3,\\,2t+1,\\,8t⟩"] ["math" "⟨2t,\\,-2t,\\,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨t+3,\\,-t-1,\\,8⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-33122" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2t+3,\\,-2t-1,\\,8⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨1-2t,\\,{t}^{2},\\,(t-1)^{2}⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t+1,\\,1-2t,\\,{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}((t-1)^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2(t-1)⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1-2t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨-2,\\,2t,\\,2t-2⟩+⟨1,\\,-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨-2,\\,-2t,\\,2t-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨-3,\\,2t+1,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-127998" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-1,\\,2t-2,\\,3{t}^{2}+2t-2⟩"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the value of $(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}$ at $t=0,$ if \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨2\\sqrt{t+1},\\,{t}^{3},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩, \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\frac{1}{3(t+1)},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, notice that\n\n$$\n(f(t)-3g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)-3{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's now find the derivatives of each function.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{t+1}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{t+1}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{t+1}⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{3(t+1)}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{3(t+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(0)-3g(0))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(0)-3{g}^{′}(0) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{0+1}},\\,3(0)^{2},\\,\\frac{1}{0+1}⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3(0+1)^{2}},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-3⟨-\\frac{1}{3},1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨0,-1,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨1,-1,0⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-1,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,-3,-2⟩"] ["math" "⟨2,1,-2⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128137" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨2,-3,-2⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Differentiate $f(t)+4g(t)$ with respect to $t$, given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{t},\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,2⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨t,\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,{t}^{4}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the constant multiple rule and the sum rule, we have\n\n$$\n(f(t)+4g(t))^{′}={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find the derivatives of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩ \\\\ {g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(f(t)+4g(t))^{′} & ={f}^{′}(t)+4{g}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+4⟨1,\\,-\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,0⟩+⟨4,\\,-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}+4,\\,\\frac{1}{t}-\\frac{4}{{t}^{2}},\\,0+16{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨2\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{{t}^{2}+1}{t},\\,2{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}},\\,8t⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{1+\\sqrt{t}}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{1}{t},\\,16{t}^{4}⟩"] ["math" "⟨\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,4{t}^{3}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70681" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨\\frac{1+8\\sqrt{t}}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,\\frac{t-4}{{t}^{2}},\\,16{t}^{3}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${(u(t)f(t))}^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ {t}^{2}+1 \\\\ 4t-7\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)={e}^{t}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n{(u(t)f(t))}^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t)\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2{t}^{3}-3) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t-7)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(u(t)f(t))}^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & ={e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}2{t}^{3}-3 \\\\ {t}^{2}+1 \\\\ 4t-7\\end{aligned}]+{e}^{t}[\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2} \\\\ 2t \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{3}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-7){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}6{t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 2t{e}^{t} \\\\ 4{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}(-5{t}^{3}-3{t}^{2}+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (3{t}^{2}-t-1){e}^{t} \\\\ (t+2){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}(4{t}^{2}+t){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}-1){e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}({t}^{2}-4t+4) \\\\ ({t}^{2}-1) \\\\ (2t+3)\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7{t}^{3}{e}^{t} \\\\ {t}^{2}{e}^{t} \\\\ 4t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-71233" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}(2{t}^{3}+6{t}^{2}-3){e}^{t} \\\\ ({t}^{2}+2t+1){e}^{t} \\\\ (4t-3){e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find  $(u(t)g(t))^{′}$ where $g(t)=⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩$ and $u(t)=2t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "By the scalar function multiple rule, we have\n \n\n$$\n(u(t)g(t))^{′}=u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${g}^{′}(t).$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\sqrt{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t+{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩ \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2t) \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)g(t))^{′} & =u(t){g}^{′}(t)+{u}^{′}(t)g(t) \\\\  & =2t⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{t}},\\,3{t}^{2},\\,1+2t⟩+2⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4\\sqrt{t},\\,6{t}^{3},\\,2t+4{t}^{2}⟩+⟨8\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,2t+2{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3}+2t,\\,4{t}^{2}+6{t}^{3}⟩"] ["math" "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨5\\sqrt{t},\\,4{t}^{3},\\,3t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,2{t}^{2},\\,10{t}^{2}⟩"] ["math" "⟨6\\sqrt{t},\\,{t}^{3},\\,t+6{t}^{2}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-128481" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨12\\sqrt{t},\\,8{t}^{3},\\,4t+6{t}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $(u(t)f(t))^{′}$ where $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]$ and $u(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar function multiple rule, we can write\n\n$$\n(u(t)f(t))^{′}={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nLet's find ${u}^{′}(t)$ and ${f}^{′}(t).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {u}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u(t)f(t))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(t)f(t)+u(t){f}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ -{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ {cos}^{2}⁡t-{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\ {e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡2t \\\\ {e}^{t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/state.json" "file_sha256" "b4f5b322733198c84d46359cde75010b298d8bee79122a21c2d613fc18db5a21"} {"question" "q-70688" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14077032/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d8917056359fc7a911c9849366c5e395853b5f615dfe124852814926eef334a1"} {"question" "q-70688" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :an